<title>HONG KONG: Reuters plans Asia editorial boost.</title>
<headline>Reuters plans Asia editorial boost.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reuters Holdings Plc said on Thursday it plans to strengthen its editorial presence in Asia in a reorganisation involving a move of editing staff to Singapore from Hong Kong early next year.</p>
<p>The world news and information group said in a statement it would strengthen its Asian reporting and editing, including its Hong Kong reporting bureau, with savings made by producing textual news, television and news pictures in a Reuters-owned building in Singapore.</p>
<p>The timing of the move was partly tied to the introduction of a new editorial production system, it said. Since last year, Reuters main technical centre for Asia has been in Singapore.</p>
